# The trial of pod-guest in podvm (T-061): crates/podvm-windows keeps
# podvm's glue and calls the crate. Its lib.rs gives settings() (the per-run
# directories `podvm-windows-PID-TAG` under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR,
# PODVM_WINDOWS_KEEP, the marker `podvm`, the OEM name `PODVM`), keeps each
# function with its podvm signature (stage, run, provision, cleanup,
# scratch_dir, RunGuard, mailbox), keeps base_cache and dos::base_cache
# (PODVM_WINDOWS_BASE, PODVM_DOS_BASE), cap_status (docker's 0 to 124) and
# dos::stage with the marker `podvm-dos`, and re-exports the rest of the
# crate. Ten files leave podvm. crates/podvm/src/windows reads a timeout
# with timeout_of and a failed nonce as a runtime error. Each podcrates tag
# moves to v0.9.0. The citations of TODO/gate.md T-1641 and the code map
# follow the moved files.
# podvm's tests of the touched crates (the windows verbs are unit tests of
# the binary); clippy of the workspace and rustfmt of the touched crates, as
# podvm's gate.yml runs them; the runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate;
# each Rust toolchain of the workflows against the rust-version of
# podcrates; and the binary `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static
# check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-windows
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-windows -p podvm --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-guest, pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-term and pod-tls at 0.9.0); the
# trial's path form has no row for them. Each other row of the patch must be
# the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
